text: >-
  On 9/11/2025. Sheriff Smith with the Utah County Sheriff's Office received a
  phone call at

  approximately 2004 hours from Sheriff Brooksby with the Washington County
  Sheriff' s

  Office. According to Sheriff Brooksby, he had received a phone call from a
  former deputy

  who had previously been employed with the Sheriff's Office. The former deputy,
  identified

  as Mike Mitchell, explained that he had received a phone call from the father
  of Tyler

  Robinson. Mike Mitchell explained that Tyler Robinson confessed to his father
  that he was

  the shooter at Utah Valley University. Tyler Robinson's parents worked with
  law

  enforcement to arrange a way for Tyler Robinson to turn himself in without a
  confrontation

  with law enforcement. Mike Mitchell coordinated with law enforcement to have
  Tyler

  Robinson meet with law enforcement at the Washington County Sheriff's Office.
  Tyler

  Robinson arrived at the Washington County Sheriff's Office accompanied by his
  parents at

  approximately 2226 hours. Tyler Robinson was not wearing clothing consistent
  with the

  clothing observed on surveillance cameras during and around the time of the
  incident at

  UVU. According to a photo provided to me by Agent Davis with the Utah State
  Bureau of

  Investigation, Tyler Robinson arrived at the Washington County Sheriff's
  Office wearing a

  dark colored hat, a maroon-colored T-shirt, jeans, and white/gray colored
  Converse style

  shoes. Tyler Robinson's mother relayed to law enforcement that Tyler Robinson
  had

  expressed having suicidal ideations. Sergeant Elsholz with the Utah State
  Bureau of

  Investigation provided me with a photograph of Tyler Robinson's Utah driver
  license. The

  driver license was taken from the person of Tyler Robinson by Agent Davis with
  the Utah

  State Bureau of Investigation.

  On 9/12/2025. at approximately 0100 hours. FBI Special Agent Lange conducted
  an

  interview with the boyfriend of Tyler Robinson at the Washington County
  Sheriff's Office.

  The boyfriend was identified as Lance Twiggs. During the interview, Lance
  showed

  investigators text messages between Tyler Robinson and himself. The following
  is the

  content of those messages between Tyler Robinson and Lance Twiggs. First
  message

  (Tyler): "I am still ok my love, but am stuck in orem for a little while
  longer yet"

  . Second

  message (Tyler): "shouldn't be long until I can come home, but I gotta grab my
  rifle still.

  To be honest I had hoped to keep this secret till I died of old age. I am
  sorry to involve

  you".

  . Third message (Lance): "you weren't the one who did it right????" Fourth
  message

  (Tyler): "I am, I'm sorry". Fifth message (Lance): "I thought they caught the
  person?"

  Sixth message (Tyler): "no, they grabbed some crazy old dude, then
  interrogated someone

  in similar clothing". Seventh message (Tyler): "I had planned to grab my rifle
  from my

  drop point shortly after, but most of that side of town got locked down. Its
  quiet, almost

  enough to get out, but theres one vehicle lingering'.
